        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best Jackery power station for most people is the Explorer 1000 v2. It is light, simple and big enough for a fridge through an evening outage or a long weekend at a campsite, and its LiFePO4 battery will outlast most of the devices you plug into it. If home backup is the main job, the HomePower 2000 Plus v2 is the better machine, with more output, double the solar input and room to grow to about 12kWh.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For camping, the Explorer 500 v2 is the sweet spot, and the 300 Plus covers devices and day trips. Only step up to the Explorer 5000 Plus if you have 240V loads and a budget for panels and an electrician. Whatever you buy, skip the old NMC Explorers, match your panels to the solar input ceiling, and register the warranty the day the box arrives.
          </p>
